"""Regions and their rulers, year by year, for the Roman page (rom/). Read by scripts/rome.py.

Each region is a group of anchor points. The page draws the Voronoi cells of all anchors and colours each cell by who
held its region at the END of the year, so the borders between regions run halfway between neighbouring anchors.
FRONTIERS adds pairs of anchors on both sides of the big river and wall frontiers, so those borders follow the line.

Years: negative = BC, positive = AD, no year 0. Ranges are inclusive. A range is (from, to, owner, note); the note
is shown in the tooltip (for "other" it names the people or state). Owner keys are listed in OWNERS in rom/index.html.
"""

# Shorthands for the long chains of eastern rulers before Rome (Persia, Alexander, his successors).
def east_chain(alex_from, then):
    """Achaemenid Persia until Alexander took the region (end of alex_from - 1), Alexander's empire to 324 BC,
    his successors' wars to 302 BC, then `then` (a list of ranges from 301 BC)."""
    return [(-509, alex_from - 1, "achaemenid", None), (alex_from, -324, "alexander", None),
            (-323, -302, "diadochi", None)] + then


